<title>PAKISTAN: Foreign investors buy Pakistani bank shares.</title>
<headline>Foreign investors buy Pakistani bank shares.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group of foreign investors led by  Sintra Fund Ltd, managed from New York, has bought a 20 percent stake in the Islamic Investment Bank Ltd, the bank said in a statement on Saturday.</p>
<p>It did not say how much the group had paid, but said five new directors had been appointed to the board.</p>
<p>The Peshawar-based bank is listed on the Karachi Stock Exchange and has a paid-up capital of 147.64 million rupees. Its 10-rupee stock closed 0.90 up at 11 on Friday.</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
